.\" khatm   manual page
.TH KHATM 1 "2026-06-14" "khatm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
khatm \- seal your books, chapter by chapter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B khatm
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ args ...]
.RB [ --json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B khatm
is a terminal study tracker. Each book is a markdown checklist; khatm tracks
what is done, what to study next (dependency- and deadline-aware), how fast
you are actually going, and whether you will hit the deadlines you set. Finish
a whole book and that is a
.IR khatma :
its spine goes on your shelf.
.PP
Run with no arguments in a terminal,
.B khatm
opens an interactive TUI. Every command also works headless, and mutating
commands accept
.B --json
for scripting.
.PP
All state is plain text: one markdown file per book plus a single append-only
log. khatm only creates files and appends lines   it never rewrites what you
wrote, so hand-editing is safe and the data is yours to grep, back up, or
version with git.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Prepare the data directory and write a sample syllabus.
.TP
.B books
List every book with its progress.
.TP
.B status
Today's summary: streak, open promises, and what to study.
.TP
.B next
The dependency- and deadline-aware suggestion for what to study, with reasons.
.TP
.BI "study " chapter
A timed session (Enter stops it). With
.B --pomo
.RI [ work / break ]
run pomodoro intervals; only focused minutes are logged.
.TP
.BI "log " "chapter duration"
Record a session manually.
.RB [ --pages
.IR N ]
.RB [ --date
.IR D ].
.TP
.BI "book new " "id " [ title ]
Start a syllabus.
.RB [ --pages
.IR N ]
.RB [ --deadline
.IR D ].
Also:
.BI "book add " "id title"
and
.BI "book section " "id title" .
.TP
.BI "goal " "target " --by " when"
Make a promise; it is priced against your recent pace before you commit.
.B goal
alone lists open promises;
.B goal --drop
.I target
drops one.
.TP
.BI "done " chapter
Seal a chapter   the ceremony. The last chapter of a book triggers the khatma.
.TP
.B review
.RI [ book ]
Spaced review of due cards. Cards become reviewable once their chapter is
sealed; grading uses SM-2.
.TP
.B cards
.RI [ book ]
List review cards and when each next falls due.
.TP
.B edit
.RI [ book ]
Open a book's markdown file (or the books directory) in
.B $VISUAL
or
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.B pace
.RI [ book ]
Burndown, ETA, and the pace required to hit your deadlines.
.TP
.B shelf
Every book you have ever sealed.
.TP
.B graph
.RI [ weeks ]
A session heatmap.
.TP
.B doctor
Dependency cycles, stale promises, and estimate bias.
.TP
.B dump
The full state as one JSON object (api version 1).
.SH SYLLABUS FORMAT
One markdown file per book under
.IR <root>/books/ .
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
# Operating Systems: Three Easy Pieces
meta: deadline=2026-08-30 pages=650

## Virtualization
- [ ] Processes ~18p
  ? what does fork() return :: 0 in child, child pid in parent
- [ ] Thread API ~10p [needs: 1, otherbook/3]
.EE
.in
.PP
.B ~18p
/
.B ~2h
/
.B ~90m
are optional estimates.
.B [needs: ...]
lists prerequisites (a chapter number, a section title, a title substring, or
.IR book/ref ).
.B "? front :: back"
lines under a chapter are spaced-review cards.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KHATM_DIR
Data directory (default
.IR ~/.khatm ).
.TP
.B EDITOR ", " VISUAL
Editor for
.BR "khatm edit" .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour.
.TP
.B KHATM_ANIM
Set to
.B 0
to disable the seal ceremony animation.
.TP
.B KHATM_ROMAN
Render the seal mark in roman letters instead of Arabic.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I <root>/books/*.md
One markdown syllabus per book.
.TP
.I <root>/log.txt
The append-only event log; all state is rebuilt from it on load.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, nonzero on error. With
.BR --json ,
failures print
.B {"ok":false,...}
and exit nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README for the full syllabus and scripting reference.
